  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img height=\"213\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/ccb73a29-11c4-4129-9698-2981c137907c.png\" width=\"208\" /></p><p>Number of covalent bond formed by Boron is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math>.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><msub><mi>BF</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mfenced><mo>-</mo></msup></math> Covalency <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo></math></p><p>The oxidation state of an element represents the charge it would have if all the bonding electrons were assigned to the more electronegative atom in the bond.</p><p>Oxidation number of fluorine is -1</p><p>Then,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>(</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></math></p><p>Oxidation state <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></math>&nbsp;for Boron</p>",
